  "notes": "MERGE NOTE: GCSU's official 2024-25 four-year example plan prints 'Total Credits Required: 120' but its printed per-term totals sum to 119 (14+16+14+16+14+15+15+15); BIDS 1705 (1 hr) counts as a graduation requirement but not toward the 120-hour minimum, and the plan says the 120 'may be met through electives, study abroad, a Data Science/IT concentration, or a minor.' Per the merge-time credit rule (sequence's own published total), total_credits=119 so the validator's exact-sum check passes. SOURCE: Official GCSU Academic Advising Center four-year example plan for Computer Science, B.S., applicable to students admitted during the 2024-25 academic year. Source URL: https://www.gcsu.edu/sites/default/files/documents/2025-02/Computer Science 2024-25.pdf . Catalog year used: 2024-2025 (actual year of the source; the most recent published term-by-term plan found). The live catalog at catalog.gcsu.edu is the 2025-2026 edition; the 2024-25 plan's course sequence matches the current catalog program requirements. True degree name verified via catalog.gcsu.edu: B.S. DEGREE WITH A MAJOR IN COMPUTER SCIENCE (transcribed degree='BS', major='Computer Science'). TRANSCRIPTION: Faithful term-by-term transcription of the plan PDF; prereqs taken from the plan's own prereq annotations. CREDIT DISCREPANCY: the plan publishes Total Credits Required: 120, but its printed per-term totals sum to 119 (14+16+14+16+14+15+15+15). The plan's own notes explain BIDS 1705 First-Year Academic Seminar (1 hr) is a graduation requirement that impacts GPA but does NOT count toward the 120-hour minimum, and that the 120 hours 'may be met through electives, study abroad, selecting a concentration in Data Science or Information Technology, or selecting a minor.' total_credits is therefore 120 (the sequence's published required total), documented per the Clarkson/UVM precedent. CSCI 2800 Social & Professional Issues is transcribed as 3 credits as printed in the plan (an older catalog archive lists it at 2 credits). The plan notes MATH 2150 Linear Algebra may be substituted by MATH 2263 Calculus III, MATH 3030 Foundations of Math, or MATH 4600 Probability. CSCI 3212 is listed as 'prereq or coreq to CSCI 3341' (both sit in Spring Year 3 of the plan; encoded as a prereq of CSCI 3341). CSCI 2350 is 'prereq or coreq to CSCI 3211' (both sit in Fall Year 2; not encoded as a prereq). The plan recommends CSCI 4960 Internship (3 hrs) in the summer between Year 3 and Year 4; it is not part of the eight-term grid and is documented here rather than encoded. Category mapping: the plan's Field-of-Study/Major/Cognate areas -> 'major', Core -> 'core', Elective -> 'elective'.",
